---
layout: changelog
title: "Project environments for development, staging, and QA"
date: 2026-11-12
cover: /images/changelog/2026-11-12.avif
tags: console, cli, sdk
---

Appwrite Cloud projects now have environments. A project can carry development, staging, and QA backends next to production, each with its own databases, storage, users, functions, sites, and settings, under the same project ID and on the same bill.

Create an environment from the new environment switcher in the project sidebar. Start it empty, or as a clone of the project that copies its structure and settings, with rows, files, and users only when you ask for them. Apps, the CLI, and the MCP server reach an environment with the project's ID plus the environment's ID, so the same code runs against production or any environment.

Free and Pro projects get five environments each, and Enterprise projects get 25 by default. Environments don't count as projects on your plan, and their usage is added to the project's.

